592 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/K 1
/P 91 0 R
/S /H1
/T (Analyzing images and videos demands attention to detail, especially when reviewing hours of recordings. AI tools, with their advanced algorithms, analyze and interpret visual data from surveillance cameras, optimizing the time and resources required. AI applications in image and video processing include enhancing visual quality for the justice system and enabling the automatic detection and tracking of objects.)
>>
endobj
593 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/K 2
/P 91 0 R
/S /H1
/T (  2. Improving Image Quality from Surveillance Cameras: AI employs techniques in the spatial and frequency domains to enhance image quality, particularly for low-quality materials like CCTV footage and mobile device videos. Forensic video analysis frameworks use advanced algorithms, such as Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization \(CLAHE\), to improve video quality for digital investigations. Investigators often begin by collecting visual materials from sources such as CCTV footage, aiming to extract as much information as possible from the crime scene.)
>>
endobj
594 0 obj
<<
/K 2
/P 92 0 R
/S /Figure
>>
endobj
595 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/K 0
/P 92 0 R
/S /H1
/T (7. Real-Time Crime Scene Analysis This technology enables investigators to collect additional information in less time, which can be crucial for solving cases. Furthermore, the precision of these measurements minimizes the risk of human error, ensuring that evidence is more reliable in court. Importantly, this method also prevents contamination or distortion of traces, as it eliminates the need for manual investigation during the initial evidence-collection phase.)
>>
endobj
596 0 obj
<<
/Alt ()
/K 1
/P 92 0 R
/S /H1
/T ( 8. Pattern and Trace Analysis Pattern analysis is a labor-intensive, subjective process that is often susceptible to human error. Forensic experts typically rely on their experience and knowledge to manually examine evidence. However, the integration of AI techniques in pattern analysis, trace analysis, and computer vision has the potential to greatly enhance the accuracy and efficiency of forensic work.)
>>
endobj
